#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# d_solve_value

#% text
# `d_solve_value(eqs, y(x), x)` gives the solution of a differential equation as an expression in `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It solves as `d_solve` does; with several solutions the result is their list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Exponential decay from 3:

#% cell
d_solve_value([y'(x) == -2*y(x), y(0) == 3], y(x), x)
#% output
#= 3*exp(-2*x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The general solution with its constants:

#% cell
d_solve_value(y''(x) + 4*y(x) == 0, y(x), x)
#% output
#= c(1)*cos(2*x) + c(2)*sin(2*x)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `d_solve` gives rules:

#% cell
d_solve([y'(x) == -2*y(x), y(0) == 3], y(x), x)
#% output
#= [[y(x) -> 3*exp(-2*x)]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `d_solve`, `n_dsolve_value`
